new file mode 100644
index 0000000..639ea75
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+# Deploying Fizzy on a single server
+
+Fizzy ships with a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org) configuration
+(`config/deploy.yml`) for running it on **one Linux server**: everything —
+the web app and the background jobs — runs in a single container, data is
+stored in SQLite, and [kamal-proxy](https://kamal-deploy.org/docs/proxy)
+terminates SSL with a Let's Encrypt certificate.
+
+```
+kamal setup   # first deploy
+kamal deploy  # every deploy after that
+```
+
+When it finishes, Fizzy is available at `https://<your-hostname>`.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server with SSH access as `root` (Kamal installs Docker on it
+  during `kamal setup` if it's missing) and ports 80/443 open.
+- A DNS record for the hostname you want to serve Fizzy from, pointing at
+  that server. Let's Encrypt needs this to issue the SSL certificate.
+- Docker and Ruby/Bundler on the machine you deploy *from*, so you can
+  build the image and run `bin/kamal`. Kamal uses a registry on that
+  machine (`localhost:5555` in `config/deploy.yml`) and the server pulls
+  the image from it over SSH, so no external container registry account
+  is needed.
+
+## 1. Fill in `config/deploy.yml`
+
+Edit the example values in `config/deploy.yml`:
+
+| Value | Replace with |
+| --- | --- |
+| `192.168.0.1` | The IP address (or SSH hostname) of your server. |
+| `fizzy.example.com` | Your hostname. It appears as `proxy.host`, `APP_HOST`, `SMTP_DOMAIN` and in `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` — all four must stay in sync. `APP_HOST` is what Rails puts in the links in emails, including the sign-in magic links Fizzy's passwordless login relies on. |
+| `smtp.example.com` | Your outgoing mail (SMTP) server, plus `SMTP_PORT` if it isn't 587. |
+| `builder.arch` | `amd64` for a typical Intel/AMD server; change to `arm64` for an ARM server. |
+
+Email matters: Fizzy logs people in with a code/link sent by email, so
+Fizzy can't sign anyone in until SMTP works. If your mail server needs no
+authentication, leave the `SMTP_USERNAME`/`SMTP_PASSWORD` secrets below
+unset; add `SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO: "false"` under `env.clear` if
+your server doesn't do STARTTLS.
+
+## 2. Set the secrets
+
+`.kamal/secrets` reads every secret from the environment of the machine
+you deploy from — the file itself contains no credentials and is safe to
+commit. Export at least:
+
+```sh
+# Signs cookies/sessions. Keep the same value across deploys and back it
+# up: changing it signs everyone out. Generate one with:
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE=$(bin/rails secret)
+
+# Your mail server credentials (if it requires authentication):
+export SMTP_USERNAME=...
+export SMTP_PASSWORD=...
+```
+
+Web Push notifications additionally need a VAPID key pair. Generate one:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+and export the two values it prints. Push is optional — Fizzy runs fine
+without it, browsers just won't receive push notifications.
+
+## 3. Deploy
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+This installs/starts kamal-proxy and Docker on the server (if needed),
+builds the image, boots the container, obtains the SSL certificate, and
+the container entrypoint creates/migrates the SQLite databases. Visit
+`https://<your-hostname>` and create the first account.
+
+Later deploys (the volume below is untouched):
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+Useful day-to-day commands: `bin/kamal logs`, `bin/kamal console`,
+`bin/kamal shell` (see `aliases` in `config/deploy.yml`).
+
+## Where the data lives (and why it survives deploys)
+
+The container mounts a single named Docker volume, `fizzy_storage`, at
+`/rails/storage`. Everything that must persist is under that directory:
+
+- the SQLite databases (`production`, cable, cache and queue — see
+  `config/database.sqlite.yml`),
+- uploaded files (local Active Storage, `storage/production/files`).
+
+Kamal replaces the container on every deploy but never removes the
+volume, so boards, cards, accounts and uploads survive. Back up that
+volume (on the server: `docker volume inspect fizzy_storage`, then copy
+its mountpoint); stop the app (`bin/kamal app stop`) or snapshot the
+SQLite files consistently when you do.
+
+Background jobs need no extra setup on this configuration: Solid Queue
+runs inside Puma in the same container (`SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA`, and it is
+Puma's default for non-SaaS Fizzy — see `config/puma.rb`), so mail
+delivery, notifications and the recurring tasks in `config/recurring.yml`
+all run on the box.
+
+## Scope
+
+This is deliberately a one-box setup: one web role on one host. Don't add
+more web hosts behind the same volume — the SQLite files and uploads on a
+local Docker volume are only visible to containers on this server. For a
+multi-server setup you'd move to MySQL and shared/object storage, which
+is what the (private-infra) SaaS configuration under `saas/` does.
diff --git a/test/deploy_config_test.rb b/test/deploy_config_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..039ca11
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/deploy_config_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+require "test_helper"
+require "yaml"
+
+class DeployConfigTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
+  DEPLOY_CONFIG = YAML.load_file(Rails.root.join("config/deploy.yml"))
+  SECRETS = File.read(Rails.root.join(".kamal/secrets"))
+
+  test "deploys a single web role to a single host" do
+    servers = DEPLOY_CONFIG.fetch("servers")
+
+    assert_equal %w[ web ], servers.keys
+    assert_equal 1, servers.fetch("web").size
+  end
+
+  test "terminates SSL at the proxy for the configured host" do
+    proxy = DEPLOY_CONFIG.fetch("proxy")
+
+    assert_equal true, proxy.fetch("ssl")
+    assert proxy.fetch("host").present?
+    assert_equal proxy.fetch("host"), DEPLOY_CONFIG.dig("env", "clear", "APP_HOST")
+  end
+
+  test "persists SQLite and uploads on a volume mounted at /rails/storage" do
+    volumes = DEPLOY_CONFIG.fetch("volumes")
+
+    assert volumes.any? { |volume| volume.end_with?(":/rails/storage") }, volumes.inspect
+  end
+
+  test "runs background jobs in the same container instead of a separate role" do
+    assert_not_equal "false", DEPLOY_CONFIG.dig("env", "clear", "SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA").to_s
+    assert_nil DEPLOY_CONFIG.dig("servers", "jobs")
+  end
+
+  test "configures an SMTP mail server" do
+    clear_env = DEPLOY_CONFIG.dig("env", "clear")
+
+    assert clear_env.fetch("SMTP_ADDRESS").present?
+    assert clear_env.fetch("SMTP_PORT").present?
+  end
+
+  test "every referenced secret is read from the environment in .kamal/secrets" do
+    secret_names = DEPLOY_CONFIG.dig("env", "secret")
+
+    assert_includes secret_names, "SECRET_KEY_BASE"
+
+    secret_names.each do |name|
+      assert_match(/^#{Regexp.escape(name)}=\$#{Regexp.escape(name)}$/, SECRETS, "expected .kamal/secrets to read #{name} from the environment")
+    end
+  end
+end
